": "Canis familiaris", "name": ["Canis familiaris", "Canis lupus familiaris"], "taxId": "9615", "abbreviation": "CFA", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "binding", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}, {"dbId": 10210537, "displayName": "Factor IIa inhibitors (peptide) bind IIa", "stId": "R-RNO-9603302", "stIdVersion": "R-RNO-9603302.1", "isInDisease": false, "isInferred": true, "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["Factor IIa inhibitors (peptide) bind IIa"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Rattus norvegicus", "inferredFrom": [9603302], "species": [{"dbId": 48895, "displayName": "Rattus norvegicus", "name": ["Rattus norvegicus", "R. norvegicus", "Rn", "brown rat", "Norway rat"], "taxId": "10116", "abbreviation": "RNO", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "binding", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}, {"dbId": 10087517, "displayName": "Factor IIa inhibitors (peptide) bind IIa", "stId": "R-MMU-9603302", "stIdVersion": "R-MMU-9603302.1", "isInDisease": false, "isInferred": true, "maxDepth": 1, "name": ["Factor IIa inhibitors (peptide) bind IIa"], "releaseDate": "2026-03-25", "speciesName": "Mus musculus", "inferredFrom": [9603302], "species": [{"dbId": 48892, "displayName": "Mus musculus", "name": ["Mus musculus", "M. musculus", "Mm", "house mouse"], "taxId": "10090", "abbreviation": "MMU", "className": "Species", "schemaClass": "Species"}], "category": "binding", "className": "Reaction", "schemaClass": "Reaction"}], "reviewed": [{"dbId": 9603358, "displayName": "G\u00f3mez-Outes, Antonio, 2018-03-21", "dateTime": "2018-03-21 14:29:59", "className": "InstanceEdit", "schemaClass": "InstanceEdit"}], "species": [48887], "summation": [{"dbId": 9603298, "displayName": "In the blood coagulation process, prothrombin is proteolytic...", "text": "In the blood coagulation process, prothrombin is proteolytically cleaved to form thrombin (factor IIa) which in turn, acts as a serine protease that converts soluble fibrinogen into insoluble strands of fibrin. Specifically, thrombin converts factor XI to XIa, factor VIII to VIIIa, factor V to Va, fibrinogen to fibrin, and factor XIII to XIIIa.<p>Direct thrombin inhibitors (DTIs) represent a new class of promising anticoagulation agents. DTIs are increasingly being used instead of heparin to provide initial, rapid anticoagulation. Unlike heparin, which requires a mediator (antithrombin) to potentiate anticoagulation, DTI peptides can inhibit free and bound thrombin directly. Lepirudin (brand name Refludan) is a recombinant hirudin derived from yeast cells (Weitz et al. 1990). Hirudin is a naturally occurring anticoagulant produced by the salivary glands of medicinal leeches. Bivalirudin (brand name Angiomax, Angiox) is a synthetic analog of hirudin, with a shorter period of binding to thrombin (Gladwell 2002). Desirudin (brand name Iprivask) is another recombinant hirudin derivative that directly inhibits free and fibrin-bound thrombin (Graetz et al. 2011).", "className": "Summation", "schemaClass": "Summation"}], "reviewStatus": {"dbId": 9821382, "displayName": "five stars", "definition": "externally reviewed", "name": ["five stars"], "className": "ReviewStatus", "schemaClass": "ReviewStatus"}, "updateTrackers": [{"dbId": 9939828, "displayName": "Update Tracker - [Reaction:9603302] Factor IIa inhibitors (peptide) bind IIa - v92:[modifyText]", "action": ["modifyText"], "updatedInstance": [9603302], "className": "UpdateTracker", "schemaClass": "UpdateTracker"}], "isChimeric": false, "category": "binding", "input": [{"dbId": 9603327, "displayName": "Factor IIa inhibitors (peptide) [extracellular region]", "stId": "R-ALL-9603327", "stIdVersion": "R-ALL-9603327.1", "maxDepth": 2, "name": ["Factor IIa inhibitors (peptide)"], "consumedByEvent": [9603302], "className": "Set", "inDisease": false, "schemaClass": "DefinedSet"}, {"dbId": 156786, "displayName": "activated thrombin (factor IIa) [extracellular region]", "s